WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.731
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.001 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme song playing]

3
00:03.420 --> 00:04.546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

4
00:04.630 --> 00:05.923
START DATING...

5
00:36.620 --> 00:40.958
BETWEEN STEPS

6
00:41.583 --> 00:43.835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS, AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:43.919 --> 00:45.546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

8
00:52.552 --> 00:54.554
[♪ pensive music plays]

9
01:02.604 --> 01:04.356
[Youjin] What are you thinking about right now?

10
01:07.192 --> 01:09.194
[♪ music fades]

11
01:10.779 --> 01:12.197
What are you thinking about?

12
01:12.864 --> 01:14.700
[hesitating] I wasn't thinking about anything.

13
01:16.827 --> 01:18.745
Wait, you feel kind of warm.

14
01:18.829 --> 01:19.830
[Minjae] Hmm?

15
01:21.039 --> 01:22.457
No, I'm not.

16
01:23.041 --> 01:24.167
[Youjin] Let me see.

17
01:25.460 --> 01:27.170
I think you have a bit of a fever.

18
01:28.589 --> 01:31.842
-That's because I have a bit of a cold. -[Youjin] Yeah.

19
01:32.384 --> 01:33.927
I just need to take medicine and...

20
01:34.011 --> 01:35.429
Yeah, I just need to take meds.

21
01:36.388 --> 01:39.016
Then eat the porridge, take your meds, and get some sleep.

22
01:39.099 --> 01:40.100
Hold on a second.

23
01:40.809 --> 01:41.810
[Minjae] Okay.

24
01:42.936 --> 01:45.147
FINAL EPISODE

25
01:45.230 --> 01:47.441
[♪ pleasant music playing]

26
01:47.524 --> 01:48.817
[Youjin] Do you have a bowl for this?

27
01:48.900 --> 01:50.068
-A bowl? -[Youjin] Yes.

28
01:50.152 --> 01:51.737
[Minjae] A bowl... Right.

29
01:54.906 --> 01:56.366
I've got two here.

30
01:56.450 --> 01:57.784
[Youjin] Just one is enough.

31
01:59.202 --> 02:00.537
Why? Aren't you going to eat?

32
02:00.620 --> 02:01.621
[Youjin] No, I'm good.

33
02:03.749 --> 02:05.625
But... Why not?

34
02:05.709 --> 02:06.960
Let's eat together.

35
02:07.711 --> 02:08.962
-Hmm? -[Youjin] Mmm-mmm.

36
02:10.172 --> 02:12.549
It's still warm. I don't think we need to heat it up.

37
02:15.552 --> 02:16.678
One moment.

38
02:24.019 --> 02:25.145
[Minjae] Thank you.

39
02:25.228 --> 02:26.897
[Youjin] You need the side dishes too, right?

40
02:26.980 --> 02:31.526
Side dishes? Side dishes...

41
02:33.445 --> 02:34.446
There's kimchi...

42
02:34.529 --> 02:36.573
[Youjin] Kimchi would be too spicy for you right now.

43
02:39.409 --> 02:40.577
Do you have a sauce dish?

44
02:40.661 --> 02:43.372
[Minjae] A sauce dish? Yeah. Hold on.

45
02:44.206 --> 02:45.666
A small dish...

46
02:47.292 --> 02:48.752
This. I have this one.

47
02:48.835 --> 02:50.170
[Youjin] Yeah, this one will do.

48
02:52.172 --> 02:53.382
You can sit down.

49
02:53.465 --> 02:54.466
[Minjae] Okay.

50
03:04.434 --> 03:05.435
[Youjin] Here.

51
03:07.562 --> 03:08.772
Eat up.

52
03:08.855 --> 03:09.856
[Minjae] Okay.

53
03:10.899 --> 03:12.818
[Youjin] If it's too bland, add some soy sauce.

54
03:13.902 --> 03:14.903
[Minjae] Okay.

55
03:20.826 --> 03:22.452
Mmm! Mmm.

56
03:24.121 --> 03:25.122
[Youjin] Hmm.

57
03:26.581 --> 03:28.166
But it's probably not bland.

58
03:30.794 --> 03:34.297
I was bawling my eyes out when I made it.

59
03:35.424 --> 03:38.009
That porridge has at least two bowls of my tears in it,

60
03:38.093 --> 03:40.679
so there's no way it's bland. It might even be too salty.

61
03:45.642 --> 03:50.564
Did you cry because you were so worried and sad when you heard I was sick?

62
03:53.024 --> 03:54.151
[Minjae snickers]

63
03:54.234 --> 03:55.360
Why are you laughing?

64
03:56.111 --> 03:57.404
Is this funny to you?

65
04:00.157 --> 04:03.160
[Minjae chuckles softly]

66
04:04.744 --> 04:05.745
[Youjin tuts]

67
04:10.917 --> 04:11.918
It's not salty.

68
04:13.044 --> 04:14.171
It's sweet.

69
04:16.673 --> 04:17.716
I'm telling the truth.

70
04:19.217 --> 04:20.302
Try it.

71
04:21.011 --> 04:23.096
It's sweet. It's really delicious.

72
04:23.180 --> 04:24.181
Here.

73
04:24.723 --> 04:26.558
Come on, just try a bite. Come on.

74
04:27.100 --> 04:28.727
-[Youjin sighs] -[Minjae] Come on.

75
04:38.862 --> 04:41.656
If you thought I forgave it all, you're wrong.

76
04:43.784 --> 04:45.786
We're not back together.

77
04:47.287 --> 04:48.622
We're not?

78
04:48.705 --> 04:50.165
[Youjin] Of course not.

79
04:50.248 --> 04:54.211
I'm super petty, okay? And I hold grudges forever.

80
04:54.294 --> 04:56.546
So don't get the wrong idea.

81
04:58.215 --> 04:59.216
[Minjae] Okay.

82
05:02.886 --> 05:03.887
[sighs]

83
05:04.429 --> 05:05.430
[sniffles]

84
05:05.514 --> 05:06.723
[Youjin] What?

85
05:06.807 --> 05:07.808
[Minjae sighs]

86
05:09.893 --> 05:11.311
I don't want to eat anymore.

87
05:16.066 --> 05:18.193
Well, we can't see each other.

88
05:19.945 --> 05:21.404
We can't do that.

89
05:23.281 --> 05:25.617
But we can talk on the phone at night.

90
05:26.952 --> 05:27.953
On the phone?

91
05:28.036 --> 05:29.037
[Youjin] Yeah.

92
05:29.704 --> 05:31.581
If you call me at night, I'll answer.

93
05:35.252 --> 05:36.586
So calling me is okay.

94
05:37.671 --> 05:40.715
And thinking about me before going to bed. You can do that too.

95
05:43.134 --> 05:46.471
And when you wake up in the morning, you can think about me first thing.

96
05:46.555 --> 05:48.265
That's okay too. You can do that.

97
05:50.559 --> 05:53.395
And you can think about me all day.

98
05:53.478 --> 05:57.566
And like me. Like me like crazy.

99
05:59.192 --> 06:01.444
Well, that one's kind of tricky, actually.

100
06:02.279 --> 06:03.905
No. Actually, you can do that.

101
06:06.241 --> 06:07.325
-[Minjae] Okay. -[Youjin] All right.

102
06:07.951 --> 06:09.536
Will you eat that porridge now?

103
06:12.789 --> 06:14.249
[Minjae] Huh? Yeah.

104
06:17.168 --> 06:21.381
But we can't get back together or start dating again.

105
06:26.136 --> 06:28.096
We can't do that?

106
06:28.179 --> 06:29.180
[Youjin] No.

107
06:30.682 --> 06:33.059
Some things you can, some things you can't.

108
06:33.143 --> 06:35.270
Sometimes this, sometimes that.

109
06:35.353 --> 06:36.479
Complicated, isn't it?

110
06:38.690 --> 06:41.651
-[Minjae sighs] -[Youjin chuckles softly]

111
06:41.735 --> 06:43.028
You're so cute.

112
06:44.988 --> 06:46.740
[cell phone vibrates]

113
06:46.823 --> 06:47.949
Hang on a second.

114
06:52.245 --> 06:53.872
It's Mom. I should head home.

115
06:54.539 --> 06:56.249
-[Minjae] Okay. -[Youjin] I'm sorry.

116
06:56.333 --> 06:59.377
[Minjae] No worries. I'll call you a taxi. One second.

117
06:59.461 --> 07:02.464
[Youjin] Don't. I can just take a bus home. It's okay.

118
07:03.131 --> 07:04.841
Then let me walk you to the bus stop.

119
07:04.924 --> 07:06.926
The bus stop is right around the corner.

120
07:07.010 --> 07:08.345
I can go by myself.

121
07:08.428 --> 07:09.471
[Minjae] But...

122
07:09.554 --> 07:12.223
Finish the porridge, take your meds, and get some rest.

123
07:12.307 --> 07:13.308
I'll call you.

124
07:13.391 --> 07:15.268
[Minjae] But... No, wait. Wait.

125
07:15.352 --> 07:17.062
Wait right there.

126
07:17.145 --> 07:18.271
Give me one second.

127
07:19.481 --> 07:21.191
-Now... -[door lock beeps]

128
07:21.274 --> 07:23.276
[♪ pleasant music turns upbeat]

129
07:29.699 --> 07:30.700
Oh.

130
07:36.539 --> 07:37.582
Youjin.

131
07:41.920 --> 07:43.088
[sighs]

132
07:53.556 --> 07:55.558
[♪ theme song playing]

133
08:03.692 --> 08:05.151
-[door closes] -[door lock beeps]

134
08:19.958 --> 08:20.959
Where are you?

135
08:21.042 --> 08:23.336
Hey, I said I'd walk you to the bus stop.

136
08:23.420 --> 08:26.089
You don't need to. I said I'm okay.

137
08:27.006 --> 08:28.007
Yeah.

138
08:29.384 --> 08:31.594
Ah. I'm almost there already.

139
08:32.637 --> 08:35.348
Yeah. I'm already at the bus stop.

140
08:36.558 --> 08:37.559
Yeah.

141
08:38.226 --> 08:39.769
I'll call you when I get home.

142
09:18.892 --> 09:19.893
-[Minjae] Hello. -[digital beeps]

143
09:19.976 --> 09:21.811
[♪ theme song continues playing]

144
09:23.521 --> 09:24.522
[Minjae grunts]

145
09:25.231 --> 09:26.232
-[Youjin] Huh? -[Minjae groans]

146
09:27.275 --> 09:28.443
Man, it's cold.

147
09:29.778 --> 09:31.196
When did you get here?

148
09:33.615 --> 09:34.949
[Minjae chuckles]

149
09:44.334 --> 09:45.502
It's cold, isn't it?

150
09:45.585 --> 09:46.586
[Minjae] Yeah.

151
09:54.761 --> 09:56.179
Do you want to listen to music?

152
09:56.971 --> 09:58.098
Yeah, I'd love to.

153
10:08.358 --> 10:09.526
Is this the right side?

154
10:10.735 --> 10:12.362
Like this. There.

155
10:25.834 --> 10:26.835
Me?

156
11:25.101 --> 11:26.102
[Minjae] Go on in.

157
11:26.186 --> 11:27.187
[Youjin] Okay.

158
11:27.270 --> 11:28.271
[Minjae] Make sure to eat.

159
11:29.063 --> 11:30.481
Bye. I'll call you.

160
11:30.565 --> 11:31.566
[Minjae] Bye.

161
11:35.653 --> 11:37.113
[Minjae exclaims softly]

162
11:40.241 --> 11:42.118
-It's cold. Go. -[Minjae] No, it's not cold.

163
11:42.202 --> 11:43.328
I'll watch you head in.

164
11:44.412 --> 11:46.873
-Bye. -[Minjae] Go.

165
11:54.672 --> 11:55.924
-[Youjin mouthing] Go. -[Minjae mouthing] Go.

166
11:56.007 --> 11:58.009
[♪ theme song ends]

167
12:02.889 --> 12:04.140
[door lock beeps]

168
12:09.562 --> 12:11.564
[♪ comical music playing]

169
12:34.379 --> 12:35.380
[gate closes]

170
12:45.265 --> 12:47.267
[♪ music fades]

171
12:47.350 --> 12:49.519
Mom, is Youjin home?

172
12:50.144 --> 12:52.021
Yeah. She just got home. Why?

173
12:52.897 --> 12:54.399
[Youseong] What do you mean, why?

174
12:54.482 --> 12:55.692
[loudly] Hey, Lim Youjin!

175
12:56.734 --> 12:58.987
It's your day off,

176
12:59.070 --> 13:01.155
and you can't even stay home for once?

177
13:01.239 --> 13:04.534
You could at least run some errands for Mom and help her out a little.

178
13:04.617 --> 13:05.952
She's got a lot on her plate.

179
13:06.035 --> 13:07.036
Come on.

180
13:07.120 --> 13:09.914
You ran one errand, and you're making a big deal out of it?

181
13:11.958 --> 13:14.210
[Youseong] Mom, I'm not saying this because I ran one errand.

182
13:14.294 --> 13:15.712
I'm telling the truth.

183
13:16.170 --> 13:17.171
Hey, Youjin.

184
13:17.255 --> 13:18.631
Come on, am I wrong?

185
13:18.715 --> 13:21.050
Didn't you bring the porridge container back home?

186
13:21.134 --> 13:23.761
I mean, the thermos you put the porridge in earlier.

187
13:23.845 --> 13:26.222
I forgot. [clears throat] I'll make sure to get it back.

188
13:26.306 --> 13:27.307
[Miyoung] Okay.

189
13:27.932 --> 13:28.933
Porridge?

190
13:30.768 --> 13:35.481
Youjin's friend is sick, so she made some porridge and went over to see her.

191
13:35.565 --> 13:37.734
Man, she didn't even get to rest on her day off.

192
13:38.568 --> 13:39.610
Her friend?

193
13:40.570 --> 13:43.156
Hey, who is this friend you even made porridge for?

194
13:45.158 --> 13:48.161
Who did you make the porridge for? I said, who is it?

195
13:48.244 --> 13:49.245
Who is this friend?

196
13:49.328 --> 13:51.164
Jeez, it's Subin.

197
13:52.707 --> 13:54.417
Subin caught a cold.

198
13:55.835 --> 13:58.796
What? Subin caught a cold?

199
13:58.880 --> 14:00.381
[Miyoung] Yeah, apparently.

200
14:00.465 --> 14:02.467
Youjin made porridge and took it to her.

201
14:04.427 --> 14:06.262
[Yongseok] Hmm. I see.

202
14:06.888 --> 14:08.514
Did she see a doctor?

203
14:08.598 --> 14:11.434
That poor girl is away from home all by herself, and she's sick?

204
14:11.517 --> 14:13.478
[Youjin] Ah. It's just a cold.

205
14:14.228 --> 14:17.023
She had the porridge and took her meds. Now, she's all better.

206
14:22.904 --> 14:24.072
[Minjae sighs]

207
14:27.158 --> 14:28.159
[chuckles softly]

208
14:33.998 --> 14:36.000
[cell phone vibrating]

209
14:42.924 --> 14:43.925
[sighs]

210
14:47.136 --> 14:49.138
[♪ jazz music playing over speakers]

211
14:59.607 --> 15:00.608
-[Minjae] Hello. -[Jihoon] Hey.

212
15:03.778 --> 15:05.321
Can we get another glass, please?

213
15:05.404 --> 15:07.490
-[staff] Oh. Got it. -[Minjae] I don't need one.

214
15:08.407 --> 15:09.575
I quit drinking.

215
15:11.577 --> 15:13.162
[Jihoon] We don't need the glass, actually.

216
15:13.246 --> 15:14.247
[staff] Got it.

217
15:17.250 --> 15:18.251
[Jihoon sighs]

218
15:21.420 --> 15:23.297
[Minjae] You said you had a favor to ask me?

219
15:25.049 --> 15:27.635
If it's something I can help you with, I will.

220
15:28.302 --> 15:30.763
If I can't, well, there's not much I can do about that.

221
15:31.556 --> 15:34.600
But I came out here to at least hear you out.

222
15:36.477 --> 15:38.604
I wanted to ask you a favor about Youjin.

223
15:41.566 --> 15:42.567
What about Youjin?

224
15:46.612 --> 15:47.613
[Jihoon] Uh...

225
15:49.490 --> 15:51.993
This is Youjin's.

226
15:53.494 --> 15:54.871
They're matching rings.

227
15:55.621 --> 15:57.623
I can't keep them forever,

228
15:58.875 --> 16:00.835
so I'd like you to give them to her.

229
16:02.837 --> 16:04.589
Well, don't get me wrong.

230
16:04.672 --> 16:07.049
They're not mine. They're Youjin's.

231
16:07.133 --> 16:08.885
She didn't give them to me.

232
16:10.469 --> 16:13.514
Well, she did give them to me,

233
16:13.598 --> 16:15.433
but she didn't mean it that way.

234
16:17.476 --> 16:19.729
I'm not explaining this very well.

235
16:21.647 --> 16:22.648
[Minjae sighs]

236
16:23.941 --> 16:27.653
If they're Youjin's, why don't you give them to her yourself?

237
16:28.613 --> 16:32.283
I can't. I can't call her right now.

238
16:33.367 --> 16:35.161
[Minjae] What do you mean, you can't call her?

239
16:35.244 --> 16:37.955
She hasn't changed her number or anything. Just call her.

240
16:38.039 --> 16:40.625
I don't need to explain every little detail to you.

241
16:40.708 --> 16:42.835
No, I'm not asking you to explain it to me.

242
16:43.711 --> 16:45.254
Just do it yourself.

243
16:48.758 --> 16:50.468
They're yours.

244
16:52.428 --> 16:55.181
Youjin bought them for your birthday.

245
16:57.558 --> 17:00.561
You're supposed to hear this from her,

246
17:00.645 --> 17:03.064
but I'm telling you because I think you misunderstand.

247
17:04.732 --> 17:06.359
What do you mean, misunderstand?

248
17:06.859 --> 17:09.028
That's... not what it is.

249
17:09.111 --> 17:11.239
Yeah, there's nothing to misunderstand, really.

250
17:12.281 --> 17:13.658
You know better than anyone

251
17:14.992 --> 17:17.870
how Youjin feels and how much she likes you.

252
17:22.124 --> 17:24.168
So do better, you jerk.

253
17:25.711 --> 17:29.715
The timing, reality, the circumstances... That's all just excuses and bullshit.

254
17:29.799 --> 17:30.841
[Minjae] It's not bullshit--

255
17:30.925 --> 17:32.301
It is, you jerk.

256
17:32.927 --> 17:35.763
Everything you're saying is about making sure you'll be loved.

257
17:36.973 --> 17:41.102
If the circumstances are right, if there's time, and if things are easier,

258
17:41.185 --> 17:45.565
then she'll love you, you'll be loved, and she won't leave.

259
17:45.648 --> 17:46.983
That's your logic.

260
17:48.568 --> 17:49.694
[Minjae sighs heavily]

261
17:50.444 --> 17:51.779
Look, forget all that.

262
17:53.197 --> 17:55.533
Think about how you can love her instead.

263
17:56.617 --> 17:57.618
[♪ gentle music playing]

264
17:57.702 --> 17:59.161
It's not hard. It's easy.

265
18:00.204 --> 18:03.666
Don't underestimate how she feels, don't dismiss her feelings.

266
18:05.835 --> 18:07.128
Be sincere with her.

267
18:08.129 --> 18:10.172
Do the things she wants you to do,

268
18:10.256 --> 18:13.467
and don't do the things she tells you she doesn't like.

269
18:15.136 --> 18:19.724
And if you don't know what she likes or doesn't like, just ask her.

270
18:20.808 --> 18:22.602
Ask her, and then just do that.

271
18:25.855 --> 18:27.732
Do you get what I'm saying?

272
18:32.028 --> 18:34.947
Jeez. Did you get it or what?

273
18:35.656 --> 18:38.200
[tuts] Why are there so many students like you here?

274
18:39.660 --> 18:41.746
Jeez, it's like talking to a monkey.

275
18:41.829 --> 18:43.748
[Minjae] What?

276
18:45.166 --> 18:47.960
Actually, you're tall, so...

277
18:48.044 --> 18:49.378
You're a chimpanzee.

278
18:50.838 --> 18:53.174
[Minjae scoffs]

279
18:54.634 --> 18:55.635
[Jihoon] I'm tired.

280
18:56.302 --> 18:57.678
[grunts] Let's go.

281
19:01.641 --> 19:02.642
[groans]

282
19:04.477 --> 19:05.770
Take that with you.

283
19:05.853 --> 19:07.355
We're going to pay now.

284
19:14.862 --> 19:15.863
[Jihoon grunts]

285
19:21.327 --> 19:24.705
All right. You said you quit drinking,

286
19:24.789 --> 19:27.708
so next time, let's grab some food instead of drinks.

287
19:28.209 --> 19:30.544
Sure. Next time, it'll be on me.

288
19:34.340 --> 19:35.508
[Jihoon] Don't you have gloves?

289
19:36.467 --> 19:37.468
Gloves?

290
19:38.761 --> 19:42.223
I lose stuff easily

291
19:42.306 --> 19:44.475
and they're uncomfortable, so I don't wear them.

292
19:48.020 --> 19:49.021
Look.

293
19:50.189 --> 19:54.568
Youjin knitted these herself

294
19:55.611 --> 19:57.196
and gave them to me for Christmas.

295
19:59.824 --> 20:00.825
[Minjae] Ah.

296
20:01.534 --> 20:02.535
[Jihoon] Now go.

297
20:58.549 --> 21:00.342
[♪ music fades]

298
21:03.929 --> 21:06.766
I know I'm the woman here, but I'm going to put my pride aside

299
21:08.100 --> 21:09.852
and make the first move.

300
21:09.935 --> 21:11.270
[♪ soft music playing]

301
21:11.353 --> 21:12.605
Park Minjae...

302
21:14.982 --> 21:15.983
I like you.

303
21:17.985 --> 21:19.779
I want you to be my boyfriend.

304
21:46.514 --> 21:48.516
[♪ music fades]

305
21:48.599 --> 21:51.352
[door opens, closes]

306
21:51.435 --> 21:53.479
[Youjin] Mom, can you hurry and get mine ready first?

307
21:53.562 --> 21:54.688
[Miyoung] Yeah, I'm almost done.

308
21:54.772 --> 21:56.440
[Youjin] Okay. I'm not going to eat much.

309
21:56.524 --> 21:57.733
-Just a little. -[Miyoung] All right.

310
21:58.567 --> 22:00.486
-I'm running late. Can you please... -[Miyoung] Fine.

311
22:00.569 --> 22:02.822
Hey, don't worry. You can take your time.

312
22:02.905 --> 22:04.865
Your brother is going to drive you to school.

313
22:06.033 --> 22:07.034
[Youjin] Huh?

314
22:10.955 --> 22:11.956
[gate opens]

315
22:13.374 --> 22:14.583
[gate closes]

316
22:21.048 --> 22:22.049
[Youseong] You sit in the back.

317
22:22.132 --> 22:23.133
[Youjin] Why?

318
22:23.217 --> 22:24.718
[Youseong] Because you get out before Subin.

319
22:25.469 --> 22:26.470
[Youjin] What?

320
22:29.974 --> 22:31.267
[car starting]

321
22:58.711 --> 23:00.004
[Youseong] Subin, get in here.

322
23:01.422 --> 23:02.882
[Youjin] No, get in here.

323
23:03.757 --> 23:04.884
[Youseong] No, here...

324
23:04.967 --> 23:06.051
-[Youjin] Come on, here. -[Subin] Okay.

325
23:06.135 --> 23:07.136
[Youseong] Get in... here.

326
23:08.470 --> 23:09.889
[Subin] Hello.

327
23:09.972 --> 23:11.473
Yeah, hello, Subin.

328
23:18.689 --> 23:21.859
You didn't have to give me a ride, though.

329
23:21.942 --> 23:23.235
I would've been fine.

330
23:23.319 --> 23:24.403
[Youjin] Hmm.

331
23:24.486 --> 23:27.615
I'm already driving Youjin anyway, so you might as well come with us.

332
23:28.657 --> 23:31.035
It's nice having someone to chat with on the way.

333
23:32.703 --> 23:35.080
[Youseong] Right. I heard you were sick, Subin.

334
23:36.332 --> 23:38.167
[Subin] Ah. Yeah.

335
23:38.876 --> 23:40.794
What about the doctor? Did you go see one?

336
23:41.503 --> 23:45.424
It wasn't that bad. It was just a cold.

337
23:45.507 --> 23:47.259
It's been so cold lately, so...

338
23:47.343 --> 23:48.344
[Youjin] Yeah.

339
23:48.427 --> 23:49.511
So I caught a cold.

340
23:49.595 --> 23:50.596
Right.

341
23:50.679 --> 23:53.349
[Youseong] I know. It's been freezing the past few days.

342
23:53.432 --> 23:56.894
Too bad you got sick, because it's supposed to stay cold.

343
23:58.729 --> 24:01.899
How about I keep giving you rides until you're feeling better?

344
24:02.483 --> 24:04.944
Uh... No, I'm fine.

345
24:05.986 --> 24:08.656
[Youseong] Well, I can just pick you up too when I give Youjin a ride.

346
24:08.739 --> 24:11.492
[Youjin] Really? Dude, you're going to give me a ride every morning?

347
24:11.992 --> 24:13.786
"Dude"? Show your brother some respect.

348
24:14.453 --> 24:16.038
Uh, I mean, sorry.

349
24:16.830 --> 24:18.999
So you're going to give me a ride every morning?

350
24:19.083 --> 24:21.752
Well, it's cold, and taking the bus can be exhausting.

351
24:21.835 --> 24:24.338
Mmm... Well, I'd love that.

352
24:26.966 --> 24:28.634
Subin, I can give you a ride too.

353
24:29.301 --> 24:31.261
Oh. Really?

354
24:33.889 --> 24:36.433
You'll really give us a ride every morning? You promise?

355
24:37.393 --> 24:39.436
Yay, I get to sleep an extra 30 minutes.

356
24:39.520 --> 24:40.896
[both chuckle]

357
24:42.022 --> 24:45.109
Subin, do you have a boyfriend?

358
24:45.192 --> 24:47.528
-Sorry? -Why would you ask something like that?

359
24:48.028 --> 24:49.780
[Youseong] Why not? What's wrong with asking?

360
24:49.863 --> 24:53.367
I was just checking to find a nice guy among my friends to set her up with.

361
24:53.450 --> 24:56.412
You don't have any nice guy friends.

362
24:57.121 --> 24:59.748
And you have no idea how popular Subin is.

363
24:59.832 --> 25:01.792
There are tons of guys lining up for her.

364
25:01.875 --> 25:03.210
No way.

365
25:03.293 --> 25:05.754
Who likes me? There's no one like that.

366
25:07.089 --> 25:10.467
Kim Sejin. He follows you around because he likes you.

367
25:11.135 --> 25:12.136
[Youseong] Kim Sejin?

368
25:13.053 --> 25:14.304
Who's Kim Sejin?

369
25:14.388 --> 25:16.473
He's a guy from my cohort in the lab.

370
25:16.557 --> 25:19.685
He's smart, but kind of a jerk.

371
25:19.768 --> 25:21.812
Hmm. There's a guy like that?

372
25:21.895 --> 25:24.106
No, he doesn't like me.

373
25:24.898 --> 25:26.817
And I don't like him either.

374
25:26.900 --> 25:30.404
No, I didn't say you liked him. I said he likes you.

375
25:30.988 --> 25:32.531
Yeah, I know.

376
25:32.614 --> 25:34.575
He doesn't like me, either.

377
25:34.658 --> 25:35.951
[♪ comical music playing]

378
25:36.035 --> 25:39.288
Anyway, there's nothing going on between you two, right?

379
25:41.248 --> 25:42.624
No.

380
25:42.708 --> 25:44.543
Nothing.

381
25:44.626 --> 25:46.837
There's absolutely nothing between us.

382
25:48.964 --> 25:51.967
If you have any nice friends, please set me up with one of them.

383
25:52.676 --> 25:53.802
Really?

384
25:54.762 --> 25:56.388
Should I set you up with my friend?

385
25:57.473 --> 25:58.932
Then how about a blind date?

386
26:00.142 --> 26:03.270
Apparently, my relative knows this guy who is a MOFE deputy director.

387
26:03.353 --> 26:06.273
He went to our school, and I hear he's a really great guy.

388
26:06.356 --> 26:09.443
Hey, Lim Youjin, don't butt in. You stay out of this.

389
26:30.839 --> 26:33.425
[Youjin] Oh, boy. Drive home safe. Bye.

390
26:41.141 --> 26:42.935
Hey. Kim Sejin.

391
26:54.363 --> 26:55.364
[Sejin sighs]

392
26:56.657 --> 26:57.699
Look, Youjin.

393
27:00.911 --> 27:06.542
I didn't mean to put you in a tough situation or anything.

394
27:06.625 --> 27:08.418
So don't get the wrong idea.

395
27:09.545 --> 27:10.838
[Youjin] The wrong idea?

396
27:10.921 --> 27:12.172
But you know what they say.

397
27:13.465 --> 27:16.009
"You make the mess, you clean it up."

398
27:17.052 --> 27:18.887
Yeah, I do.

399
27:18.971 --> 27:21.140
You think I wouldn't know that saying?

400
27:21.223 --> 27:22.224
It's not that.

401
27:24.476 --> 27:25.978
Anyway, I... [clearing throat]

402
27:26.728 --> 27:31.441
[inhales] I believe the one who caused the problem should be the one to fix it.

403
27:33.735 --> 27:35.487
So you need to...

404
27:37.114 --> 27:38.407
deal with your problem.

405
27:39.950 --> 27:41.702
What are you talking about?

406
27:43.787 --> 27:44.913
You'll know soon enough.

407
27:51.461 --> 27:54.047
By the way, wasn't it... Subin in the car just now?

408
27:55.632 --> 27:56.633
Yeah, it was.

409
27:56.717 --> 27:58.969
[Sejin exclaims softly] I forgot to reach out to her.

410
28:02.180 --> 28:04.474
Hey, didn't you two have a thing going on?

411
28:06.727 --> 28:07.978
There's nothing going on.

412
28:08.061 --> 28:10.314
We're just friends. Just friends.

413
28:10.397 --> 28:11.899
[Youjin] I see.

414
28:11.982 --> 28:14.276
Subin said there's nothing between you two, either.

415
28:15.110 --> 28:17.654
That's what Subin said? That there's nothing between us?

416
28:17.738 --> 28:18.739
[Youjin] Yeah.

417
28:19.823 --> 28:21.450
And Subin is going on a blind date.

418
28:23.160 --> 28:24.161
What?

419
28:24.953 --> 28:28.165
Well, we know this guy who is a deputy director at the MOFE.

420
28:28.248 --> 28:30.834
And when I offered to set them up, she said yes.

421
28:39.968 --> 28:40.969
[sighing] Damn it.

422
28:42.721 --> 28:43.931
[cell phone vibrates]

423
28:45.766 --> 28:47.976
[Sejin] Subin, are you going on a blind date?

424
28:48.060 --> 28:49.603
[♪ light music playing]

425
28:49.686 --> 28:50.687
YES

426
28:50.771 --> 28:51.772
SEND

427
28:52.439 --> 28:53.440
[Subin] Yes.

428
28:58.737 --> 28:59.821
[cell phone vibrates]

429
29:01.156 --> 29:02.449
[Sejin] Why?

430
29:03.867 --> 29:06.078
[mumbles] What does he mean, "Why?"

431
29:11.959 --> 29:13.669
It's none of your business, isn't it?

432
29:24.721 --> 29:26.431
[cell phone vibrating]

433
29:29.184 --> 29:30.769
INCOMING CALL KIM SEJIN

434
29:33.188 --> 29:34.606
Aren't you going to answer that?

435
29:40.988 --> 29:42.155
It's a spam call.

436
29:43.824 --> 29:45.534
POWER OFF

437
29:46.326 --> 29:47.536
[line ringing]

438
29:47.619 --> 29:48.787
[automation] The phone is turned off.

439
29:48.870 --> 29:51.206
You will now be connected to voicemail...

440
29:51.289 --> 29:52.290
[line disconnects]

441
30:09.516 --> 30:11.059
[Taeho coughing]

442
30:17.107 --> 30:18.191
[cell phone vibrates]

443
30:19.234 --> 30:20.902
[Sejin] I'm going to head out.

444
30:20.986 --> 30:22.029
[Taeho] Huh?

445
30:22.112 --> 30:23.363
Are you going somewhere?

446
30:23.864 --> 30:25.741
[Sejin] Ah. Library. To the library.

447
30:25.824 --> 30:27.826
[Taeho] Hey, before you head off to the library...

448
30:27.909 --> 30:29.911
-Hey, could you... -[Hangyeol] Hey, where are you...

449
30:29.995 --> 30:31.621
No, I need to head out right now.

450
30:31.705 --> 30:34.374
-[Taeho] Hey! That little... -[Hangyeol] But...

451
30:36.960 --> 30:38.045
[Taeho] Hey.

452
30:38.128 --> 30:39.129
[door closes]

453
30:39.629 --> 30:40.630
[Chansoo] Hey.

454
30:42.049 --> 30:43.050
Hey!

455
30:43.967 --> 30:44.968
[Chansoo grunts]

456
30:48.096 --> 30:49.097
[Hangyeol] Hey...

457
30:49.723 --> 30:50.891
Youjin.

458
30:50.974 --> 30:52.559
-[Youjin] Yes? -[Hangyeol] Are you busy?

459
30:52.642 --> 30:54.352
-You're not? No? -[Youjin] No.

460
30:54.436 --> 30:57.731
Well, I just have something to ask you.

461
30:57.814 --> 30:58.815
What?

462
30:59.232 --> 31:02.360
[Hangyeol] I don't know if I should ask this, though.

463
31:04.071 --> 31:07.407
It's not really okay to pry into someone's personal life, right?

464
31:07.991 --> 31:10.911
Mmm... Of course not. Why would you even ask?

465
31:10.994 --> 31:13.080
Yeah, right? That's what I thought too.

466
31:13.705 --> 31:16.333
[Chansoo] How is that personal? It's a team matter.

467
31:16.416 --> 31:17.542
It is personal.

468
31:17.626 --> 31:20.378
[groans] Enough, Hangyeol. Forget it. [tuts]

469
31:22.255 --> 31:24.257
Youjin. So...

470
31:24.883 --> 31:27.552
Whether it's personal or not, I...

471
31:28.595 --> 31:33.308
Actually, even if it's personal, I need to know this.

472
31:34.309 --> 31:35.310
Excuse me?

473
31:35.393 --> 31:37.896
Is it true that you and Minjae used to date?

474
31:40.524 --> 31:45.320
I need to know the truth so I know how to handle this.

475
31:47.697 --> 31:50.575
Is it true or not? Just tell me that. Give me a straight answer.

476
31:54.955 --> 31:56.915
[telephone ringing]

477
31:56.998 --> 31:59.042
-Right. Answer the phone first. -[Youjin] Uh...

478
32:02.129 --> 32:03.255
Yes. Hello?

479
32:05.298 --> 32:07.050
Yes, Professor. This is Youjin.

480
32:08.260 --> 32:09.261
What?

481
32:11.263 --> 32:12.264
Right now?

482
32:16.351 --> 32:17.435
[knock on door]

483
32:17.519 --> 32:18.520
[Jaehong] Yes.

484
32:19.688 --> 32:20.730
[door opens]

485
32:25.861 --> 32:27.737
Have a seat. Mmm.

486
32:28.947 --> 32:33.451
So I asked to see you because I wanted to ask you something.

487
32:35.662 --> 32:38.415
I'm not good at beating around the bush, so I'll be straight.

488
32:39.708 --> 32:41.668
I hear you and Minjae used to date.

489
32:44.754 --> 32:45.755
Is it true?

490
32:49.134 --> 32:53.221
Did you two date in secret and break up while Minjae was doing his postdoc abroad?

491
32:55.432 --> 32:57.684
Well, I'm not trying to pry

492
32:58.518 --> 33:01.438
into your personal life just to gossip.

493
33:02.480 --> 33:05.567
I'm asking because it could cause problems in our lab.

494
33:05.650 --> 33:08.737
We didn't do anything that could be problematic for the lab.

495
33:09.487 --> 33:11.615
So it's true that you two used to date?

496
33:12.365 --> 33:15.911
Yes, we used to date, but we didn't do anything that could be problematic.

497
33:15.994 --> 33:17.495
Dating in the lab...

498
33:19.539 --> 33:24.419
when you're supposed to be studying is problematic in itself.

499
33:26.046 --> 33:27.047
[Jaehong sighs heavily]

500
33:27.130 --> 33:29.966
If you're going to date, do it right and get married.

501
33:31.343 --> 33:34.346
But no. You broke up, you fought,

502
33:34.429 --> 33:37.390
you vomited blood, and you ended up in the hospital. I mean...

503
33:38.141 --> 33:39.142
[sighs]

504
33:39.643 --> 33:40.727
What is this?

505
33:42.437 --> 33:44.773
Isn't all that disrupting the academic environment

506
33:44.856 --> 33:46.483
and bringing down the whole lab?

507
33:50.445 --> 33:53.114
Of course, I'm not saying this is all your fault.

508
33:53.198 --> 33:57.077
It takes two to tango, as they say. Minjae was in the wrong, too.

509
33:57.160 --> 34:01.456
He's older, and as your senior, he should've known better.

510
34:03.333 --> 34:05.168
That said... [smacks lips]

511
34:07.087 --> 34:10.340
You see, it'd be easier for you to move

512
34:11.716 --> 34:13.176
than Minjae.

513
34:13.843 --> 34:16.012
You've got less weighing you down.

514
34:17.764 --> 34:18.765
Pardon?

515
34:20.058 --> 34:21.101
Move?

516
34:21.184 --> 34:23.144
[smacks lips] You're almost done with your master's,

517
34:23.228 --> 34:25.397
so you can finish it here.

518
34:26.856 --> 34:29.401
But after that, consider transferring to another school.

519
34:30.360 --> 34:34.281
[scoffs] But I didn't do anything bad enough to get kicked out of school.

520
34:34.364 --> 34:35.949
[Jaehong] No, you're not getting kicked out.

521
34:36.616 --> 34:38.868
I'll write you the recommendation letters and all.

522
34:38.952 --> 34:40.412
What... No.

523
34:42.330 --> 34:45.375
[sighs] Then I'd rather you make this an official matter

524
34:45.458 --> 34:47.377
and determine who's right and who's wrong.

525
34:48.920 --> 34:52.674
I'll take responsibility for my wrongs, and accept any punishment from the school.

526
34:52.757 --> 34:54.384
That would be going too far.

527
34:55.343 --> 34:57.596
No, I don't think that's necessary.

528
34:57.679 --> 35:00.056
Yes, I do think it's necessary.

529
35:00.140 --> 35:02.434
I'll make this official and take the punishment.

530
35:03.018 --> 35:05.186
[Jaehong] No, I mean... Youjin.

531
35:05.270 --> 35:07.272
This isn't the US.

532
35:07.772 --> 35:10.734
It'll be awkward for two exes to be around each other.

533
35:10.817 --> 35:12.277
The whole idea was just...

534
35:13.361 --> 35:15.905
that one of you could be considerate of the other.

535
35:16.948 --> 35:19.826
Exactly. Why should I be the one to be considerate?

536
35:19.909 --> 35:21.161
It's not awkward for me.

537
35:21.244 --> 35:23.371
Well, Minjae vomited blood.

538
35:24.748 --> 35:25.749
[sighs]

539
35:25.832 --> 35:27.917
I'm asking for your sympathy. You...

540
35:28.501 --> 35:30.670
[exhales] Youjin, you...

541
35:33.632 --> 35:36.426
Don't you feel bad for Minjae?

542
35:37.761 --> 35:40.138
No, I don't feel bad for him at all.

543
35:40.221 --> 35:41.306
Oh, really?

544
35:43.308 --> 35:46.102
All right, then. Let's ask Minjae to leave.

545
35:46.186 --> 35:49.272
Would that make you feel better? Would you really be okay with that?

546
35:50.023 --> 35:51.024
[Jaehong sighs]

547
35:52.233 --> 35:53.568
I'm saying,

548
35:54.986 --> 35:56.279
you're a nice person,

549
35:58.073 --> 36:00.575
so you should give a little.

550
36:01.242 --> 36:04.871
[scoffs] I'm not nice. And actually...

551
36:07.415 --> 36:10.585
Minjae said he'd quit school anyway.

552
36:11.378 --> 36:12.462
What?

553
36:12.545 --> 36:15.048
He said he's quitting school and quitting robotics, too.

554
36:15.131 --> 36:17.300
He's going to Canada or Toronto or wherever.

555
36:17.842 --> 36:21.596
He's quitting school and robotics because he got dumped by a woman?

556
36:22.263 --> 36:23.848
This bastard's lost his mind.

557
36:25.934 --> 36:28.812
When you date someone, you can get dumped.

558
36:28.895 --> 36:30.730
Has he ever even been in a relationship?

559
36:33.483 --> 36:35.443
Did he seriously say that?

560
36:35.527 --> 36:37.153
That he's going to quit school?

561
36:37.237 --> 36:38.697
[Youjin] You should ask him yourself.

562
36:40.573 --> 36:41.866
[Jaehong] What a crazy bastard.

563
36:43.952 --> 36:46.955
[doctor] You haven't vomited blood since then, have you?

564
36:47.038 --> 36:48.039
No.

565
36:48.123 --> 36:49.541
GASTROENTEROLOGIST JEONG YEONGJU

566
36:49.624 --> 36:52.585
And no black or red stools? No abdominal pain?

567
36:52.669 --> 36:53.670
[Minjae] No.

568
36:53.753 --> 36:55.922
And no dizziness or anything?

569
36:56.005 --> 36:57.006
No.

570
36:57.507 --> 36:59.884
[doctor] But you have a slight fever.

571
36:59.968 --> 37:01.511
Yes, I have a bit of a fever.

572
37:01.594 --> 37:04.139
[doctor] Mmm... And you've been feeling fatigued overall.

573
37:04.222 --> 37:05.223
Yes.

574
37:05.306 --> 37:07.142
[doctor] Looks like you've lost some weight, too?

575
37:08.101 --> 37:11.604
I've only been eating porridge lately, so that's probably why.

576
37:11.688 --> 37:12.814
[doctor] Mmm...

577
37:15.108 --> 37:18.278
Uh, do you have a cough or any phlegm?

578
37:18.737 --> 37:22.031
[Minjae] Mmm... No, I don't think I have a cough.

579
37:22.615 --> 37:23.867
[doctor] Hmm...

580
37:25.660 --> 37:28.413
Could you lift your shirt up a little?

581
37:34.252 --> 37:35.253
All right.

582
37:36.629 --> 37:37.797
Breathe in.

583
37:37.881 --> 37:38.882
[Minjae inhales]

584
37:39.758 --> 37:41.259
Slowly breathe out.

585
37:41.342 --> 37:43.011
[Minjae exhales]

586
37:43.094 --> 37:46.306
-[doctor] And breathe in again. -[Minjae inhales]

587
37:47.682 --> 37:49.934
-[doctor] And breathe out. -[Minjae exhales]

588
37:52.228 --> 37:53.271
[sniffles]

589
37:53.354 --> 37:55.440
[doctor] Let's get a chest X-ray.

590
37:56.316 --> 37:58.902
But I don't have a cough. Why an X-ray?

591
37:58.985 --> 38:01.905
[doctor] Yeah. Just to take a look and make sure everything's okay.

592
38:02.405 --> 38:04.032
[machine whirring]

593
38:06.242 --> 38:09.078
[staff] Breathe in and hold your breath for a moment.

594
38:09.162 --> 38:11.164
[♪ pensive music playing]

595
38:12.165 --> 38:14.626
All right, done. You can breathe now.

596
38:14.709 --> 38:16.586
-You can leave the room now. -[Minjae] Okay.

597
38:16.669 --> 38:18.671
X-RAY ROOM

598
38:50.328 --> 38:52.330
[♪ music fades]

599
38:54.374 --> 38:56.376
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY

600
39:24.028 --> 39:25.655
What are you doing here?

601
39:25.738 --> 39:29.659
Uh, I told you earlier I'd be waiting here.

602
39:29.742 --> 39:32.370
[Subin] I told you I didn't know when I'd finish.

603
39:34.747 --> 39:38.418
You said you didn't know when you'd finish, but it'd be late.

604
39:38.501 --> 39:41.212
So I could either wait or not, or just do whatever I wanted.

605
39:41.296 --> 39:43.715
-So I've been waiting-- -When I said you could either...

606
39:44.799 --> 39:48.177
[sighs] That's not what I meant.

607
39:48.261 --> 39:49.262
[Sejin] Oh.

608
39:50.805 --> 39:53.892
It seems I misunderstood.

609
39:55.310 --> 39:56.352
I'm sorry.

610
40:02.901 --> 40:06.237
So what did you want to say to me?

611
40:06.946 --> 40:08.114
Go ahead and say it.

612
40:08.781 --> 40:10.491
You said you wanted to say something.

613
40:11.075 --> 40:13.703
Why don't we go somewhere inside first...

614
40:13.786 --> 40:15.163
Have you eaten yet?

615
40:15.246 --> 40:17.665
[Subin] Yes, I had dinner earlier.

616
40:18.541 --> 40:19.542
[Sejin] Oh...

617
40:21.044 --> 40:24.005
What is it you wanted to say to me? Just tell me here.

618
40:31.721 --> 40:34.599
I'm just curious...

619
40:36.434 --> 40:38.227
why you're going on a blind date.

620
40:39.145 --> 40:40.146
What?

621
40:41.856 --> 40:42.899
[Subin sighs]

622
40:43.358 --> 40:46.527
What do you mean, why? I'm just doing it.

623
40:47.362 --> 40:48.363
I mean,

624
40:49.572 --> 40:53.701
someone like you doesn't need to go on blind dates.

625
40:53.785 --> 40:56.454
You could be with anyone you want.

626
40:56.537 --> 40:57.538
What?

627
40:58.247 --> 40:59.749
What does that even mean?

628
41:01.209 --> 41:04.170
Are you saying I'd date just anyone?

629
41:04.253 --> 41:06.297
[sighs] No, that's not what I mean.

630
41:15.848 --> 41:17.725
Honestly, I've...

631
41:20.728 --> 41:22.438
never met anyone

632
41:23.898 --> 41:25.817
as beautiful as you in my life.

633
41:28.403 --> 41:30.071
You're seriously the most beautiful person

634
41:31.197 --> 41:32.323
I've ever seen in my life.

635
41:34.325 --> 41:36.369
Celebrities, singers, idols...

636
41:37.370 --> 41:38.788
There are plenty of people everyone says are beautiful,

637
41:40.164 --> 41:42.083
but honestly, none of them even come close.

638
41:44.127 --> 41:47.046
I mean, if I'm being really generous here,

639
41:47.630 --> 41:50.008
sure, beauty is subjective,

640
41:50.091 --> 41:52.760
and everyone has their own type.

641
41:54.554 --> 41:57.056
But someone who's as smart, kind,

642
41:57.140 --> 41:59.684
considerate, and compassionate as you are...

643
42:01.894 --> 42:04.063
Seriously, I swear on my life,

644
42:05.106 --> 42:06.482
there's no one else like that.

645
42:08.401 --> 42:10.611
So why would someone like you go on a blind date?

646
42:12.071 --> 42:14.323
You don't need to do that.

647
42:15.450 --> 42:19.662
You could just pick anyone you like and date them.

648
42:20.621 --> 42:22.832
I seriously don't understand why you'd want to go

649
42:22.915 --> 42:24.834
meet some complete stranger like that.

650
42:34.385 --> 42:35.386
Do you...

651
42:37.138 --> 42:38.556
really think so?

652
42:39.140 --> 42:40.933
[voice breaking] Yes, I really think so.

653
42:42.185 --> 42:45.438
-[sniffles, sobs] -[Subin sighs]

654
42:49.400 --> 42:50.526
Then if...

655
42:52.278 --> 42:55.198
I said I wanted to date you, Sejin, would you date me?

656
42:58.618 --> 43:00.620
[♪ gentle music playing]

657
43:03.956 --> 43:06.667
What's wrong? You don't want to?

658
43:19.639 --> 43:20.640
I just...

659
43:24.435 --> 43:25.561
I feel like...

660
43:28.022 --> 43:29.273
my heart's going to burst...

661
43:32.110 --> 43:33.736
[chuckling] ...and I'm gonna die.

662
43:43.746 --> 43:44.831
[Subin chuckles softly]

663
43:48.835 --> 43:50.670
-[Sejin sobs, chuckles] -[Subin chuckles]

664
44:05.726 --> 44:06.894
[door opens]

665
44:16.195 --> 44:18.489
You haven't eaten yet? What have you been doing?

666
44:19.574 --> 44:21.159
I had so much to go over today.

667
44:21.242 --> 44:23.161
I was too busy to even think about eating.

668
44:23.244 --> 44:25.329
Even if you're busy, you can't skip meals.

669
44:25.413 --> 44:26.414
[Youjin chuckles]

670
44:27.248 --> 44:28.749
You should have some too.

671
44:28.833 --> 44:31.002
No, I've already eaten. I'm fine. Eat up.

672
44:31.502 --> 44:33.212
-Eat with me anyway. -No.

673
44:34.589 --> 44:37.800
[Youjin] Is it still too soon to eat raw fish?

674
44:37.884 --> 44:38.885
Maybe you can't eat it yet?

675
44:39.343 --> 44:40.887
[Minjae] Uh... [chuckles]

676
44:44.682 --> 44:46.017
[Youjin] You went to the hospital today, right?

677
44:46.100 --> 44:48.060
Did the doctor say you're okay now?

678
44:49.061 --> 44:50.062
[Minjae] Yeah.

679
44:50.897 --> 44:53.399
Come on, eat first. I'll tell you when you're done.

680
44:57.069 --> 44:59.030
[chuckles softly] I'm done.

681
44:59.697 --> 45:00.698
I'm really done.

682
45:03.701 --> 45:04.827
[Minjae sighs heavily]

683
45:06.204 --> 45:09.999
-So, as for the endoscopy... -[Youjin] Mmm-hmm.

684
45:11.792 --> 45:14.253
They said the bleeding's stopped and it's healing well.

685
45:15.254 --> 45:16.422
That's great to hear.

686
45:19.508 --> 45:20.676
What's up?

687
45:20.760 --> 45:22.929
Is there something else?

688
45:23.012 --> 45:24.013
[Minjae] Hmm?

689
45:24.847 --> 45:25.848
[sighs]

690
45:28.142 --> 45:30.895
Well, I have a bit of a fever.

691
45:31.479 --> 45:34.690
And since I've had surgery for lung cancer before,

692
45:34.774 --> 45:36.359
they wanted to check a few things,

693
45:36.442 --> 45:38.903
and they wanted to do a chest X-ray.

694
45:39.904 --> 45:42.156
I see. So did you do it?

695
45:42.865 --> 45:43.866
Yeah. And...

696
45:44.867 --> 45:46.744
apparently, there's a nodule in my lung.

697
45:47.828 --> 45:49.080
They said they won't know

698
45:49.163 --> 45:52.291
if it's just a lump or cancer until they do a biopsy.

699
45:53.167 --> 45:55.086
I'll get the results next week.

700
45:57.129 --> 45:58.506
I'm sure it isn't.

701
45:59.632 --> 46:03.052
Well, even if it's cancer, you can get it treated.

702
46:04.595 --> 46:05.596
[Minjae] Yeah.

703
46:06.097 --> 46:07.098
[Youjin] Yeah.

704
46:09.725 --> 46:10.726
I'm sorry.

705
46:12.687 --> 46:14.313
Sorry for what?

706
46:14.397 --> 46:15.982
You didn't do anything wrong.

707
46:17.525 --> 46:20.319
I know. I didn't do anything wrong, so why am I so unlucky?

708
46:22.321 --> 46:24.031
[Minjae sighs heavily]

709
46:24.115 --> 46:26.284
If I died now,

710
46:28.494 --> 46:30.496
I'd die without having accomplished anything,

711
46:30.579 --> 46:31.998
with nothing to leave behind.

712
46:32.081 --> 46:33.916
[chuckling] God, it'd all feel so pointless.

713
46:35.501 --> 46:36.502
[Youjin] Yeah.

714
46:40.881 --> 46:44.135
[Minjae] What you said the other day. Is it true?

715
46:45.761 --> 46:46.762
What?

716
46:47.763 --> 46:50.266
That you'd rather die than break up with me?

717
46:52.560 --> 46:54.937
Yeah, I really meant it.

718
46:57.231 --> 47:00.067
Seriously, what are you going to do if I die?

719
47:02.987 --> 47:04.697
[smacks lips] Then,

720
47:04.780 --> 47:06.741
-I'll die too. -[Minjae chuckles softly]

721
47:15.249 --> 47:16.667
I'm serious.

722
47:16.751 --> 47:18.711
I'm really going to die too.

723
47:18.794 --> 47:20.171
Come on. [chuckles dryly]

724
47:20.254 --> 47:21.547
Don't be ridiculous.

725
47:28.554 --> 47:29.555
[Youjin sobs softly]

726
47:30.222 --> 47:32.224
[♪ emotional music playing]

727
47:34.977 --> 47:35.978
I'm sorry.

728
47:36.479 --> 47:37.772
-Hey, I'm sorry. That was wrong. -[Youjin sobs]

729
47:37.855 --> 47:40.691
Come here. Come. Don't cry.

730
47:40.775 --> 47:44.653
I'm sorry. Okay? I'm sorry.

731
47:47.239 --> 47:48.240
[Youjin whimpers]

732
47:59.543 --> 48:03.798
But don't hate me, okay? Okay?

733
48:04.340 --> 48:05.841
-[Youjin sniffles] -[Minjae] Don't hate me.

734
48:07.093 --> 48:08.427
[Youjin] I don't hate you.

735
48:09.428 --> 48:11.430
[Youjin sobs]

736
48:12.181 --> 48:13.557
I love you.

737
48:16.018 --> 48:17.436
I love you.

738
48:46.340 --> 48:47.633
[Youjin] What are you thinking about?

739
48:48.134 --> 48:49.135
[Minjae] Hmm?

740
48:50.845 --> 48:52.930
Why do you keep looking elsewhere when I'm right here by your side?

741
48:54.056 --> 48:55.307
Look at me.

742
48:56.225 --> 48:57.226
[Minjae chuckles softly]

743
49:00.688 --> 49:02.773
I'm going with you to the hospital on Tuesday.

744
49:04.358 --> 49:05.609
Aren't you going to work?

745
49:05.693 --> 49:07.570
No, I can take the afternoon off.

746
49:10.030 --> 49:12.741
No, you don't need to come. I'll just call you.

747
49:13.868 --> 49:16.036
No, I'm going to go with you.

748
49:16.120 --> 49:17.872
I'd worry too much if you went alone.

749
49:21.500 --> 49:22.751
That's our taxi, right?

750
49:23.752 --> 49:24.795
[Minjae] Yeah, it is.

751
49:32.261 --> 49:33.262
Aren't you coming?

752
49:33.345 --> 49:34.346
[Minjae] Youjin.

753
49:36.474 --> 49:37.683
I think this is it for us.

754
49:42.104 --> 49:44.607
I really regretted hurting you back then.

755
49:46.317 --> 49:48.944
Then I promised myself I'd be really good to you.

756
49:49.778 --> 49:52.031
But I guess we were meant to be this way.

757
49:52.114 --> 49:53.365
There's nothing to be done.

758
49:55.743 --> 49:57.203
Still, I'm glad that we at least

759
49:57.286 --> 50:00.039
get to say goodbye face-to-face this time. Right?

760
50:00.122 --> 50:02.750
Come on. Why are you doing this again?

761
50:02.833 --> 50:03.834
I...

762
50:05.002 --> 50:06.921
don't deserve to be with you.

763
50:07.004 --> 50:08.130
I have no right to be.

764
50:08.756 --> 50:09.757
[Youjin sighs]

765
50:10.424 --> 50:12.885
Who gets to decide if you have the right to be with me?

766
50:12.968 --> 50:16.388
It's not God. It's not Buddha. It's me.

767
50:16.472 --> 50:17.890
I gave you that right.

768
50:17.973 --> 50:20.309
Just like me. I said you could love me.

769
50:21.018 --> 50:23.145
I get why you're doing this,

770
50:23.229 --> 50:25.272
but maybe the results will show it's nothing.

771
50:25.356 --> 50:27.816
And if it really is cancer, then we'll get it treated.

772
50:27.900 --> 50:28.984
I'll be with you. Okay?

773
50:29.068 --> 50:32.112
Yeah, well, that's not as easy as you think, okay?

774
50:32.905 --> 50:37.701
A devoted woman staying by the side of some poor guy who's dying?

775
50:38.285 --> 50:40.788
That's the kind of thing you see in novels and movies.

776
50:40.871 --> 50:44.124
It's easy to say you'll take care of someone who's dying. But it's not.

777
50:46.502 --> 50:48.337
I decide whether it's easy or not.

778
50:48.420 --> 50:49.588
What if I die?

779
50:50.339 --> 50:53.217
What would happen then? What would happen to you?

780
50:54.260 --> 50:57.471
Will you spend your whole life looking back on all our happy memories?

781
50:57.555 --> 50:59.181
Crying every day?

782
50:59.265 --> 51:01.350
I told you, if you die, I'll die too.

783
51:01.433 --> 51:03.269
[yells] Don't be such a child!

784
51:03.352 --> 51:05.688
-You're not dying, okay? You... -[Youjin sighs in frustration]

785
51:06.939 --> 51:08.691
Do you even know what it means to die?

786
51:09.525 --> 51:10.693
[Youjin sighs heavily]

787
51:10.776 --> 51:12.319
-God... -Listen.

788
51:13.696 --> 51:17.366
Even if it's not me, you'll find someone to spend the rest of your life with.

789
51:18.033 --> 51:21.579
So stop being so stubborn. Stop acting like a child, for God's sake!

790
51:21.662 --> 51:23.414
And you stop lecturing me.

791
51:24.248 --> 51:26.750
Are you my mom? My dad? Who are you to lecture me?

792
51:26.834 --> 51:29.753
You... I'm your senior. So yes, I can lecture you.

793
51:29.837 --> 51:32.006
In the lab, yes, but we're out in public now!

794
51:32.089 --> 51:33.299
Hey!

795
51:33.382 --> 51:34.675
[Youjin sighs] Okay, fine.

796
51:34.758 --> 51:36.343
[exhales] All right, fine.

797
51:37.177 --> 51:40.389
Let's wait for the results for now, and then we'll talk, okay?

798
51:40.973 --> 51:42.933
If it's nothing, we're good.

799
51:43.017 --> 51:46.478
-If not, we'll talk again then. Okay? -[taxi honks]

800
51:46.562 --> 51:50.733
Well... it won't make any difference, okay?

801
51:50.816 --> 51:52.985
Even if I somehow get through this one,

802
51:53.068 --> 51:56.113
I'll have to go back in six months and get tested all over again.

803
51:56.196 --> 51:57.448
[Youjin] Fine. Let's go for now--

804
51:57.531 --> 51:59.283
Then after those six months?

805
51:59.366 --> 52:01.410
-I get another six months. -[Youjin sighs]

806
52:02.411 --> 52:05.914
And I'll still be wondering, "When will it come back? When will I die?"

807
52:05.998 --> 52:08.709
I'll spend my whole life on a razor's edge.

808
52:08.792 --> 52:12.588
That's the kind of miserable life I'll have to live.

809
52:12.671 --> 52:14.965
Nothing's going to change. So...

810
52:16.550 --> 52:18.636
-[scoffs] -[Minjae] Let's end this.

811
52:21.639 --> 52:23.307
I really want to stop doing this.

812
52:23.390 --> 52:25.392
This isn't some sacrifice or act of devotion!

813
52:25.976 --> 52:30.898
I just need you in my life to be happy. That's why...

814
52:30.981 --> 52:33.150
That's why I'm trying and fighting for this.

815
52:34.735 --> 52:36.695
And you're acting like you know what's best.

816
52:36.779 --> 52:38.864
You have all this courage to break up with me,

817
52:38.947 --> 52:41.075
but you don't have the courage to fight for me?

818
52:42.201 --> 52:44.703
God, not again. How can you do this again...

819
52:46.080 --> 52:47.956
[groans] I can't believe this is happening.

820
52:48.040 --> 52:49.375
[taxi honks]

821
52:50.167 --> 52:51.168
[sighing in exasperation]

822
52:55.923 --> 52:57.925
[♪ somber music playing]

823
53:26.620 --> 53:28.622
[Youjin sobbing]

824
54:31.769 --> 54:33.771
[Minjae sobbing]

825
55:36.166 --> 55:37.251
[nurse] Mr. Park Minjae.

826
55:37.334 --> 55:38.335
[Minjae] Yes.

827
55:43.048 --> 55:45.050
[♪ music fades]

828
55:45.133 --> 55:46.343
[doctor] All right.

829
55:47.094 --> 55:48.470
If you look here,

830
55:48.554 --> 55:53.141
you can see two three-centimeter nodules in the lung. Uh...

831
55:53.225 --> 55:54.601
So we did a biopsy, and...

832
55:54.685 --> 55:56.144
THORACIC SURGEON SONG GIYEOL

833
55:56.228 --> 55:59.189
The results confirm that they are cancerous.

834
56:01.775 --> 56:04.611
The squamous cell carcinoma has recurred.

835
56:06.446 --> 56:09.116
They're not that large, but...

836
56:09.199 --> 56:10.576
I do think you'll need surgery.

837
56:11.952 --> 56:14.871
The concern is that this is the site of the recurrence,

838
56:14.955 --> 56:17.583
and it seems the cancer has already started to spread.

839
56:17.666 --> 56:19.918
So we'll need to perform open-chest surgery

840
56:20.002 --> 56:22.963
and remove the entire lower lobe of your left lung.

841
56:23.046 --> 56:25.340
Doctor, it's not a difficult surgery, is it?

842
56:25.424 --> 56:26.425
That's...

843
56:26.508 --> 56:28.635
The surgery will remove all the cancer, right?

844
56:28.719 --> 56:30.429
He'll be okay after that, right?

845
56:30.512 --> 56:33.765
[Giyeol] Uh, well... Uh...

846
56:33.849 --> 56:36.184
When can he get the surgery?

847
56:36.768 --> 56:37.769
[Giyeol] Mmm.

848
56:38.353 --> 56:41.023
Well, let's see what we can schedule.

849
56:42.190 --> 56:44.026
Yeah. Okay.

850
57:14.431 --> 57:17.184
[automation] The outer-circle train

851
57:17.267 --> 57:21.021
bound for Seongsu Station is now arriving.

852
57:21.980 --> 57:25.984
The doors are opening. Please watch your step.

853
57:26.068 --> 57:33.033
Please watch your step.

854
57:33.116 --> 57:40.082
Please watch your step.

855
57:48.715 --> 57:50.717
[♪ emotional music playing]

856
59:03.832 --> 59:05.208
[Minjae] Do you want some strawberries?

857
59:13.842 --> 59:15.343
Which one do you think is better?

858
59:19.556 --> 59:20.891
Which one do you like better?

859
59:23.935 --> 59:25.187
-This one? -[Minjae] This one?

860
01:00:37.092 --> 01:00:41.137
ARC LAB RESEARCH ASSISTANT RECRUITMENT

861
01:00:41.221 --> 01:00:43.306
NO PRIOR EXPERIENCE OR KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED

862
01:00:43.390 --> 01:00:45.976
ASSISTANT PROFESSOR PARK MINJAE OF MECHANICAL ENGINEERING

863
01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:49.688
[Minjae] All right, today, we're going to continue from where we left off last time

864
01:00:49.771 --> 01:00:53.483
and take a closer look at systems of linear equations.

865
01:00:54.234 --> 01:00:57.737
Now, the key to a system of linear equations ultimately comes down

866
01:00:57.821 --> 01:01:01.324
to what constant values B the unknowns X map to.

867
01:01:01.408 --> 01:01:05.245
If all the constants on the right-hand side are zero,

868
01:01:05.328 --> 01:01:08.623
we call it a homogeneous system, right?

869
01:01:10.041 --> 01:01:13.378
In that case, we're always guaranteed to have the trivial solution,

870
01:01:13.461 --> 01:01:15.797
where all the unknowns are zero.

871
01:01:15.881 --> 01:01:19.342
Well, I've met him, and he seemed like a nice guy.

872
01:01:19.426 --> 01:01:20.969
Come on, he's fine.

873
01:01:21.052 --> 01:01:22.888
[♪ music fades]

874
01:01:22.971 --> 01:01:25.932
Try all you want, but parents can't win against their own kids.

875
01:01:30.353 --> 01:01:32.647
What mother misses the pre-wedding family meeting?

876
01:01:35.275 --> 01:01:38.236
Are you really going to meet your son-in-law at the wedding?

877
01:01:43.366 --> 01:01:44.618
Are you really not coming?

878
01:01:51.416 --> 01:01:52.792
Suit yourself.

879
01:01:54.169 --> 01:01:56.046
Go ahead and break your daughter's heart.

880
01:01:59.049 --> 01:02:00.050
[door opens]

881
01:02:01.760 --> 01:02:03.053
[door closes]

882
01:02:03.970 --> 01:02:05.013
Mom's not coming?

883
01:02:05.555 --> 01:02:07.432
[Yongseok] Well, she says she has a terrible headache

884
01:02:07.515 --> 01:02:08.642
and just can't make it.

885
01:02:09.351 --> 01:02:10.685
Her head hurts too much.

886
01:02:13.480 --> 01:02:15.023
Let's just go without her.

887
01:02:15.106 --> 01:02:16.566
Mom can join next time.

888
01:02:18.151 --> 01:02:19.152
Is that okay?

889
01:02:19.861 --> 01:02:21.821
Sure. There will be a next time.

890
01:02:21.905 --> 01:02:23.156
It's okay. Let's go.

891
01:02:33.625 --> 01:02:34.626
[door closes]

892
01:03:05.865 --> 01:03:06.866
[sighs heavily]

893
01:03:14.958 --> 01:03:15.959
Gosh.

894
01:03:23.967 --> 01:03:25.510
[mumbling] Let's go.

895
01:03:25.593 --> 01:03:28.722
I'll just face it. I'll see.

896
01:03:29.514 --> 01:03:32.350
Yeah. We left early in case of traffic.

897
01:03:33.393 --> 01:03:34.602
Yeah, exactly.

898
01:03:36.104 --> 01:03:37.564
But my mom...

899
01:03:38.523 --> 01:03:40.984
Never mind. We'll talk when you're here.

900
01:03:41.067 --> 01:03:43.236
-[camera shutter clicks] -Where are you? Are you almost here?

901
01:03:43.319 --> 01:03:46.322
Ah. I'm almost there.

902
01:03:46.406 --> 01:03:50.535
I should be there in about five to ten minutes.

903
01:03:51.995 --> 01:03:53.329
Okay. Yeah.

904
01:03:54.581 --> 01:03:55.665
Bye.

905
01:03:57.125 --> 01:03:58.126
[line disconnects]

906
01:03:59.002 --> 01:04:00.712
[staff] Here's the bouquet you ordered.

907
01:04:00.795 --> 01:04:03.423
Yes. Thank you.

908
01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:04.758
-Thank you. -No problem.

909
01:04:04.841 --> 01:04:05.925
[Minjae] Bye.

910
01:04:53.098 --> 01:04:54.474
[motorcycle honks]

911
01:04:55.016 --> 01:04:56.059
[Minjae] Oh, no.

912
01:04:57.102 --> 01:04:58.103
[Miyoung] Oh, my.

913
01:04:58.186 --> 01:04:59.187
Are you okay?

914
01:04:59.270 --> 01:05:00.271
[Miyoung] Yeah, I'm okay.

915
01:05:01.606 --> 01:05:03.316
-Thank you. -No, not at all.

916
01:05:03.399 --> 01:05:05.235
-[Miyoung] Thank you so much. -Are you really okay?

917
01:05:05.318 --> 01:05:06.736
[Miyoung] Yes, I'm okay.

918
01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:07.904
[Minjae] Okay.

919
01:05:07.987 --> 01:05:09.864
-[Miyoung gasps] Oh, no. I'm so sorry. -[Minjae] No, don't worry.

920
01:05:09.948 --> 01:05:12.033
Hey, maybe we got here too early.

921
01:05:13.409 --> 01:05:15.203
It's better to be early than late.

922
01:05:16.329 --> 01:05:17.705
It's almost time.

923
01:05:25.255 --> 01:05:26.548
[cell phone vibrates]

924
01:05:32.887 --> 01:05:35.056
[Minjae] Sorry. I think I'll be about 10 minutes late.

925
01:05:36.141 --> 01:05:39.018
-[chuckling] I'm sorry. -No, I'm really fine. Are you okay?

926
01:05:39.102 --> 01:05:40.395
I'll pay for the flowers.

927
01:05:40.478 --> 01:05:42.605
-No. Seriously, no... -No, seriously, let me pay.

928
01:05:42.689 --> 01:05:44.566
-It was my mistake. -No, it was me.

929
01:05:47.819 --> 01:05:50.071
How tall are you, by the way?

930
01:05:50.155 --> 01:05:54.325
-My height? About 186 or 187, I think. -[Miyoung gasps]

931
01:05:54.868 --> 01:05:56.452
Ah. [chuckles]

932
01:05:56.536 --> 01:05:59.205
My son is short.

933
01:05:59.289 --> 01:06:01.624
It's not like he didn't eat, but he just didn't grow.

934
01:06:01.708 --> 01:06:03.960
-[Minjae] Oh. -I'm so jealous. [chuckles]

935
01:06:06.713 --> 01:06:08.965
Well, just like the old folks used to say,

936
01:06:09.048 --> 01:06:13.136
-you're as handsome as paint. -[staff chuckles]

937
01:06:13.219 --> 01:06:14.971
-Am I right? [chuckles] -[staff] Yes. [chuckles]

938
01:06:15.054 --> 01:06:17.265
[Minjae chuckles shyly, mumbles] Thank you.

939
01:06:18.349 --> 01:06:19.350
[Miyoung] Mmm.

940
01:06:20.393 --> 01:06:21.769
-Ah... -[Minjae] Yes?

941
01:06:21.853 --> 01:06:25.023
Since you're so tall and handsome,

942
01:06:25.106 --> 01:06:27.400
do you work as a model, or work in show business?

943
01:06:27.483 --> 01:06:30.486
Oh, no, no. Nothing like that.

944
01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:33.198
I'm just teaching students, kids at school.

945
01:06:33.698 --> 01:06:35.700
You're a teacher? [gasps]

946
01:06:35.783 --> 01:06:37.285
My goodness.

947
01:06:41.623 --> 01:06:42.624
[sighs]

948
01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:45.627
[muttering] There are guys like this out there,

949
01:06:45.710 --> 01:06:48.004
and why did she have to...

950
01:06:50.006 --> 01:06:52.967
[chuckles awkwardly]

951
01:06:56.054 --> 01:06:58.306
My daughter is tall.

952
01:06:58.389 --> 01:07:00.475
-[Minjae] Oh... -And pretty.

953
01:07:00.558 --> 01:07:03.770
She's pretty and smart. She goes to Seohan National University.

954
01:07:03.853 --> 01:07:05.939
-[chuckles softly] -[♪ soft music playing]

955
01:07:06.022 --> 01:07:07.690
Seohan National University?

956
01:07:08.942 --> 01:07:10.985
Yes. She's going to grad school there.

957
01:07:11.069 --> 01:07:14.530
She's doing a PhD in mechanical engineering.

958
01:07:14.614 --> 01:07:16.866
She wants to become a professor.

959
01:07:20.119 --> 01:07:21.120
[Minjae] Oh.

960
01:07:24.290 --> 01:07:27.919
Do you have a girlfriend? Are you in a relationship?

961
01:07:28.586 --> 01:07:31.798
-I do. Yes, I have a girlfriend. -[Miyoung] Mmm.

962
01:07:33.007 --> 01:07:37.637
So these flowers must be for her, then.

963
01:07:37.720 --> 01:07:40.682
No, I bought those for her mother...

964
01:07:41.474 --> 01:07:42.475
Her mother?

965
01:07:42.558 --> 01:07:43.601
Yes.

966
01:07:43.685 --> 01:07:45.019
My goodness. [gasps]

967
01:07:46.729 --> 01:07:47.730
[exclaims softly]

968
01:07:48.314 --> 01:07:51.901
She's so lucky to have you buying her things like this.

969
01:07:52.777 --> 01:07:53.778
[Minjae] Hmm...

970
01:07:54.320 --> 01:07:55.530
[staff] Your bouquet is ready.

971
01:07:55.613 --> 01:07:57.490
Okay. How much is it? I...

972
01:07:57.573 --> 01:07:59.117
Yes. That'll be 55,000 won.

973
01:07:59.200 --> 01:08:01.577
-[Miyoung] Let me... -Are you, by any chance...

974
01:08:02.912 --> 01:08:04.789
Youjin's mother?

975
01:08:04.872 --> 01:08:07.959
Oh, my gosh! How do you know my daughter's name?

976
01:08:09.168 --> 01:08:11.296
Hello, I'm Park Minjae.

977
01:08:11.379 --> 01:08:12.380
[Miyoung] What...

978
01:08:13.047 --> 01:08:15.133
Yes, I'm Park Minjae.

979
01:08:15.216 --> 01:08:16.634
[♪ light thrilling music playing]

980
01:08:16.718 --> 01:08:17.885
Hello.

981
01:08:17.969 --> 01:08:20.096
Where are you? How far away are you?

982
01:08:24.392 --> 01:08:25.727
Right outside the restaurant?

983
01:08:25.810 --> 01:08:28.604
There. Yeah, come in.

984
01:08:36.654 --> 01:08:37.655
Hey, I'm here.

985
01:08:37.739 --> 01:08:39.741
[♪ pleasant music playing over speakers]

986
01:08:45.747 --> 01:08:46.748
[Youjin] Yeah, this way.

987
01:08:52.670 --> 01:08:53.671
[Minjae] Hello.

988
01:08:56.507 --> 01:08:58.009
[Youseong] Mom, you said you weren't coming.

989
01:08:59.427 --> 01:09:01.012
How did you two come together?

990
01:09:01.721 --> 01:09:04.307
Hello. We met in front of the restaurant.

991
01:09:04.390 --> 01:09:07.435
I didn't recognize her at first because I'd never met her before.

992
01:09:07.518 --> 01:09:10.313
I was so surprised when I realized it was her. Right, Ms. Seo?

993
01:09:10.396 --> 01:09:11.397
[Miyoung chuckles dryly]

994
01:09:18.696 --> 01:09:21.532
It turns out Youjin got her beauty from her mother.

995
01:09:22.367 --> 01:09:24.160
That's how I recognized her right away.

996
01:09:26.079 --> 01:09:28.581
Ah. My mother will be here in a minute too.

997
01:09:30.625 --> 01:09:32.710
[whispering] He's polite and nice, isn't he?

998
01:09:33.378 --> 01:09:34.379
[whispering] I don't know.

999
01:09:35.963 --> 01:09:37.840
-[knock on door] -[staff] Your guest is here.

1000
01:09:37.924 --> 01:09:38.925
[Minjae] Okay.

1001
01:09:40.468 --> 01:09:41.469
[Youseong and Yongseok] Oh.

1002
01:09:42.303 --> 01:09:43.805
-[Youjin] Oh. -[Minjae] You're here.

1003
01:09:43.888 --> 01:09:44.889
-[Youseong] Hello. -[Miyoung grunts]

1004
01:09:47.183 --> 01:09:48.184
[Eunjoo] Let's sit.

1005
01:09:51.437 --> 01:09:53.106
I'm sorry I'm late.

1006
01:09:53.189 --> 01:09:55.733
I tried to get here sooner, but traffic was terrible.

1007
01:09:55.817 --> 01:09:58.444
Don't worry about it. We just got here too.

1008
01:10:00.363 --> 01:10:01.698
-[Minjae] All right. Let's sit. -[Eunjoo] Okay.

1009
01:10:01.781 --> 01:10:02.782
[Yongseok] Oh.

1010
01:10:10.164 --> 01:10:11.874
[Youseong sighs]

1011
01:10:11.958 --> 01:10:13.793
This is my father.

1012
01:10:14.585 --> 01:10:16.504
-[Eunjoo] Okay. -Hello.

1013
01:10:16.587 --> 01:10:18.131
I'm Youjin's father.

1014
01:10:18.214 --> 01:10:19.674
Yes. Nice to meet you.

1015
01:10:19.757 --> 01:10:22.218
-And this is my mother. -Yes, hello.

1016
01:10:22.969 --> 01:10:24.220
This is my brother.

1017
01:10:24.303 --> 01:10:26.472
-Hello. I'm Youjin's brother. -Nice to meet you.

1018
01:10:30.935 --> 01:10:31.936
[inhales]

1019
01:10:32.478 --> 01:10:35.189
It's spring, but it's still pretty chilly, isn't it?

1020
01:10:35.273 --> 01:10:37.400
Should we order some hot tea first?

1021
01:10:37.483 --> 01:10:38.484
Yes.

1022
01:10:40.278 --> 01:10:41.529
[bell dings]

1023
01:10:47.577 --> 01:10:48.870
[Yongseok inhales sharply]

1024
01:10:48.953 --> 01:10:52.582
By the way, have we met before?

1025
01:10:52.665 --> 01:10:54.500
I feel like we've met before.

1026
01:10:55.376 --> 01:10:58.671
I'm not sure. This is my first time seeing you.

1027
01:11:04.135 --> 01:11:05.219
-[Youjin tuts] -[Minjae huffs]

1028
01:11:05.303 --> 01:11:08.139
How could she lie like that without even batting an eye?

1029
01:11:09.182 --> 01:11:11.601
Well, I wouldn't call it lying.

1030
01:11:11.684 --> 01:11:15.313
She was just pretending not to know, given the situation.

1031
01:11:15.396 --> 01:11:18.316
I mean, she could've just owned up to it and apologized.

1032
01:11:18.399 --> 01:11:19.525
Why'd she have to lie?

1033
01:11:20.151 --> 01:11:22.528
Well, I said it's not lying.

1034
01:11:23.571 --> 01:11:25.656
And you?

1035
01:11:25.740 --> 01:11:28.242
You shouldn't talk about your mother-in-law like that.

1036
01:11:29.285 --> 01:11:31.245
Will you keep siding with her instead of me?

1037
01:11:32.413 --> 01:11:33.623
[chuckling] No.

1038
01:11:34.874 --> 01:11:36.292
Sorry.

1039
01:11:38.461 --> 01:11:39.587
You better behave.

1040
01:11:40.213 --> 01:11:42.131
Okay. I will.

1041
01:11:42.215 --> 01:11:44.509
[♪ pleasant music builds]

1042
01:11:44.592 --> 01:11:47.345
[groans] I was so nervous. Now I'm tired.

1043
01:11:47.845 --> 01:11:48.971
[Youjin grunts]

1044
01:11:49.055 --> 01:11:50.389
-Get some rest. -[Youjin] Okay.

1045
01:11:50.473 --> 01:11:51.516
Get some shut-eye.

1046
01:11:51.599 --> 01:11:53.142
Let me close my eyes for a bit.

1047
01:11:53.226 --> 01:11:54.227
[Minjae] Yeah.

1048
01:12:09.283 --> 01:12:10.576
What are you thinking about?

1049
01:12:13.788 --> 01:12:14.789
Me?

1050
01:12:18.334 --> 01:12:19.669
About kissing you.

1051
01:12:21.045 --> 01:12:23.464
[Youjin chuckles]

1052
01:12:30.137 --> 01:12:32.139
[♪ lively music playing]

1053
01:13:22.023 --> 01:13:25.943
BETWEEN STEPS

1054
01:14:32.677 --> 01:14:37.181
AHN PANSUK

1055
01:14:41.644 --> 01:14:45.648
THE END
